# The plant that pays six percent to put its generator thirty metres from its
# reactor.
#
# Three heat pipes in series, two percent lost at each, and the throttle turned
# down to 30% so that what arrives is what one exchanger can actually boil.
# Every design in experiment 06 asked what a plant should contain; this one
# asks where it should be, which is a question the drawing could not previously
# tell you the answer to.
#
# In experiment 08 it is the design that shows what routing looks like when
# there is somewhere to route to: a lagged main on supports, the length of the
# plot, four metres up.

machine "Long Reach"
brief power

reactor   R1  at 0,0   throttle 30

heatpipe  HP1 at 5,1
heatpipe  HP2 at 11,1
heatpipe  HP3 at 17,1

exchanger HX1 at 23,0
turbine   T1  at 27,0
generator G1  at 31,0

pump      W1  at 23,4

wire R1.heat -> HP1.in
wire HP1.out -> HP2.in
wire HP2.out -> HP3.in
wire HP3.out -> HX1.heat

wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
